===== Status =====
This device is supported in backfire 10.03 when using the brcm-2.4 branch and the proprietary wl-mimo broadcom wireless driver.
It also works using the brcm47xx branch and the open source b43 driver.

**Attitude Adjustment (12.09) with 802.11g support:** First download the [[http://downloads.openwrt.org/attitude_adjustment/12.09/brcm47xx/generic/openwrt-brcm47xx-squashfs.trx|openwrt-brcm47xx-squashfs.trx]] image. If your router will be offline while you're configuring it (e.g. if the computer you're configuring from is not co-located with your source of internet) download the associated [[http://downloads.openwrt.org/attitude_adjustment/12.09/brcm47xx/generic/packages/kmod-b43_3.3.8%2b2012-09-07-3_brcm47xx.ipk|kmod-b43]] and [[http://downloads.openwrt.org/attitude_adjustment/12.09/brcm47xx/generic/packages/kmod-cfg80211_3.3.8%2b2012-09-07-3_brcm47xx.ipk|kmod-cfg80211]] packages for offline installation. Flash the image using OpenWrt's web interface, [[toh:asus:wl-500g_deluxe#oem_installation_using_the_tftp_method|tftp]], or the Asus firmware update utility. If the router is connected to the internet, install the two mentioned packages through the router's web interface (System -> Software); otherwise manually install packages by sending them to the router's "/tmp" folder using scp then ssh over and install them using "opkg install file.ipk". Once the packages are shown as installed under the web interface (System -> Software), reboot the router, and enable wireless networking via the web interface (Network -> Wifi).

As of Attitude Adjustment 12.09, 802.11n is working.  For installation, refer to [[docs:techref:hardware:soc:soc.broadcom.bcm47xx#wifi_drivers|the bcm47xx platform's page]]


